id: interface/meaning
title: "/meaning"
kind: cognition-handle
status: active
spec_version: v1
updated: 2026-09-26

function: "separate attributed state, possibility, desire, optional target, and typed lacuna"

asks:
  - what does this mean to the observer
  - what possible state is visible
  - what is the lacuna
  - what is desired, feared, called, avoided, or unknown

output:
  state_snapshots: []
  possibilities: []
  desires: []
  target_conditions: []
  lacunae: []
  status_dimensions:
    modal: "actual | possible | predicted | counterfactual"
    motivational: "desired | feared | neutral"
    epistemic: "reported | observed | inferred | assumed | supported | disputed | unknown | unproven"

relations:
  - type: overlaps
    target: dave/meaning/model.yawn
    note: "Dave's working model of what this handle is for; a view of the principal, not a rival definition."

clarification_2026_09_26:
  recorded_by: agent-on-behalf
  recorded_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-26, from the New -> Pulse -> Meaning amendment and the sprint elevation review"
  invariants:
    - "Saving a source is not processing it; processing is not choosing; choosing is not authorizing; authorizing is not experiencing."
    - "Rank the contribution of an item to this meaning, for this observer, here; never the item's worth."
    - "A pass may change nothing; holding still is a valid result."
    - "A concept is not an artifact; a described practice is not an attempted one."
    - "Different context is not disputed: two readings kept for different contexts stay current, and where each applies stays explicitly unresolved until stated."
    - "Whose expression, who generated a reading and who accepted it are three relationships; acceptance does not make a reading true or grant permission."
  status_note: "status v1 was a version marker in the lifecycle field; it is now status: active with spec_version: v1."

compatibility: >
  possible_kind remains readable only at legacy edges. It must not mix modal,
  motivational, or epistemic meaning in canonical records.

proof:
  source:
    - readme.yawn
    - core/lacuna.yawn
  status: seed-backed
